### 3️⃣ Step 1 – Add the button & confirmation modal

**Assumption**: You already have a user profile page (e.g. `pages/account.js`).

```tsx
// pages/account.tsx  (add before the closing </div> or wherever you want it)

import { useState } from 'react';
import { useRouter } from 'next/router';
import { supabase } from '../utils/supabaseClient'; // your client

export default function Account() {
  const router = useRouter();
  const [showConfirm, setShowConfirm] = useState(false);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
  const [error, setError] = useState('');

  async function deleteAccount() {
    setLoading(true);
    setError('');
    const res = await fetch('/api/deleteAccount', { method: 'POST' });
    const data = await res.json();
    setLoading(false);
    if (data.success) {
      // signed out already in API, so reload for home
      router.push('/');
    } else {
      setError(data.error || 'Something went wrong');
    }
  }

  return (
    <div>
      {/* ...your existing account UI... */}

      <button
        className="mt-4 bg-red-600 text-white px-3 py-2 rounded"
        onClick={() => setShowConfirm(true)}
      >
        Delete my account
      </button>

      {/* Confirmation modal */}
      {showConfirm && (
        <div className="fixed inset-0 flex items-center justify-center bg-black/50">
          <div className="bg-white p-6 rounded shadow">
            <p className="mb-4 text-red-600">
              Are you sure you want to delete your account? This is permanent.
            </p>
            <button
              className="mr-4 bg-gray-300 px-3 py-1 rounded"
              onClick={() => setShowConfirm(false)}
            >
              Cancel
            </button>
            <button
              className="bg-red-600 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded"
              onClick={deleteAccount}
              disabled={loading}
            >
              {loading ? 'Deleting…' : 'Yes, delete account'}
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      )}

      {error && <p className="mt-2 text-red-600">{error}</p>}
    </div>
  );
}
```

**What we did**

- Added a red button that opens a modal.
- The modal asks for confirmation.
- On confirm it calls `/api/deleteAccount` (the secure server function we’ll create next).

> **Save point**: Commit this file or zip the project.  
> The app should still run the same; no data is touched yet.

